[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/17976029","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/1364#issuecomment-17976029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1364","id":17976029,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3OTc2MDI5","user":{"login":"trustin","id":173918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzkxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin","html_url":"https://github.com/trustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-05-16T01:29:07Z","updated_at":"2013-05-16T01:29:07Z","body":"Thanks for reporting a bug.  A workaround I can think of is to make a non-composite copy first and then duplicate the copy multiple times assuming this bug affects only `DefaultCompositeByteBuf`.  \n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/17976029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"trustin","id":173918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzkxOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin","html_url":"https://github.com/trustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/18034510","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/1364#issuecomment-18034510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1364","id":18034510,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE4MDM0NTEw","user":{"login":"dkartaschew","id":2052368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTIzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2052368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew","html_url":"https://github.com/dkartaschew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dkartaschew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-05-16T22:58:44Z","updated_at":"2013-05-16T22:58:44Z","body":"Hi, No problem on the bug report. As someone who does other F/OSS stuff on the side, it's the only way to know when something is broken. ;)\n\nWe've implemented our own patch for this issue, and it has resolved it for our own use case. (I won't warrant it's fixed it for all use cases).\n\nIn `DefaultCompositeByteBuf`, we removed the two variables `lastAccessed` and `lastAccessedId`, and rewrote `findComponent()` and `toComponentIndex()` as follows:\n\n``` java\n    @Override\n    public int toComponentIndex(int offset) {\n        assert !freed;\n        checkIndex(offset);\n        for (int i = 0; i < components.size(); i++) {\n            Component c = components.get(i);\n            if (offset >= c.offset && offset < c.endOffset) {\n                return i;\n            }\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    private Component findComponent(int offset) {\n        assert !freed;\n        checkIndex(offset);\n        for (int i = 0; i < components.size(); i++) {\n            Component c = components.get(i);\n            if (offset >= c.offset && offset < c.endOffset) {\n                return c;\n            }\n        }\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"unknown offset?\");\n    }\n```\n\nWe also removed references to those variables in `updateComponentOffsets()` and elsewhere as needed.\n\nWhile I acknowledge the above replacements are not as performant as the originals, they are essentially stateless so should allow multiple threads access to the duplicates without issues. (I've used a for loop in the `findComponent()` method to avoid creating an iterator on `components`.) \n\nWe also considered writing a `duplicate()` method as an alternative, but we got the above working quicker, and requires less deeper knowledge of netty.\n\nPS. You're free to use the above replacements if desired without restriction.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/18034510/reactio